Statistical Analysis
Pearson correlation analysis was used to investigate relationships between song popularity and audio characteristics.
Rather than relying solely on visual patterns, the analysis considers both:
Correlation coefficient
p-value
This approach helps assess whether observed relationships between variables — such as danceability and popularity — are statistically meaningful within the dataset.

Machine Learning — Genre Classification
A supervised machine learning model was developed to determine whether a song's genre can be predicted from its audio characteristics.
Model Objective
The classification task predicts one of three major cleaned genre categories:
Hip-Hop
Latin
Pop
Features Used

The model uses the following song characteristics:
Beats Per Minute
Energy
Danceability
Loudness
Liveness
Valence
Song Length
Acousticness
Speechiness
Popularity
ML Workflow

The machine learning pipeline includes:
Genre cleaning and standardization
Feature selection
Removal of Other genre records
Train/test split
Stratified sampling to preserve genre proportions
Random Forest model training
Genre prediction
Model evaluation using:
Accuracy
Confusion Matrix
Precision
Recall
F1-score
Feature importance analysis
Random Forest Classifier
A Random Forest Classifier with 200 estimators was trained to classify songs based on their audio characteristics.
RandomForestClassifier(
    n_estimators=200,
    random_state=42
)

Model Performance
The model achieved an overall accuracy of 88.89% on the test set.
Metric	Score
Accuracy	88.89%
Macro Precision	0.94
Macro Recall	0.83
Macro F1-Score	0.86
Weighted F1-Score	0.88
Classification Performance
Genre	Precision	Recall	F1-Score
Hip-Hop	1.00	1.00	1.00
Latin	1.00	0.50	0.67
Pop	0.83	1.00	0.91

The confusion matrix showed that the model correctly classified all Hip-Hop and Pop samples in the test set, while some Latin songs were classified as Pop.

Feature Importance
Random Forest feature importance was used to identify which audio characteristics contributed most to genre classification.
The feature-importance analysis provides an additional layer of interpretation by showing which characteristics were most useful to the model when distinguishing between genres.
Note: Because the dataset is relatively small, the 88.89% accuracy should be interpreted cautiously. The model demonstrates the application of classification techniques and feature analysis, but a larger dataset would provide a more reliable assessment of real-world genre prediction performance.

